      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 14-year-old boy had arm pain after a traumatic event. An X-ray showed a supracondylar process of the humerus, which is a coincidental finding but sometimes has clinical consequences. It may compress the median nerve or brachial artery, leading to symptoms. Resection can give complete relieve of symptoms."},
